WEBVTT

00:03.545 --> 00:05.171
The petrification beam

00:05.755 --> 00:08.799
is going to engulf the entire Earth
from North America!

00:08.800 --> 00:11.760
Yes... Even if we destroy humanity,

00:11.761 --> 00:15.390
in the end we'll save everyone,
and that's how we'll win!

00:16.141 --> 00:19.727
<i>How many minutes until
the petrification beam gets here?</i>

00:19.728 --> 00:23.939
Maybe, if the ones in North America
succeed in their mission...

00:23.940 --> 00:27.277
Not "if" they succeed,
they're already doing it!

00:27.861 --> 00:32.072
They'll succeed! We've got to believe
and place all our bets on them!

00:32.073 --> 00:34.534
So it's like on Treasure Island...

00:35.118 --> 00:38.412
<i>We just have to nail Senku's countdown...</i>

00:38.413 --> 00:42.125
and toss the revival fluid right
as the beam hits, right?

00:42.917 --> 00:44.251
Yes!

00:44.252 --> 00:47.838
But since the petrification beam
speeds up as it gets bigger,

00:47.839 --> 00:51.175
the timing will mostly come down to luck.
It's a one in a million chance.

00:51.176 --> 00:53.803
All up to Senku's luck, huh?

00:56.097 --> 00:59.099
In that case,
it's going to be insanely tedious,

00:59.100 --> 01:01.852
but there's definitely a way
to cover you with the Revival Fluid!

01:01.853 --> 01:03.897
Using some kind of scientific mechanism...

01:14.741 --> 01:17.494
No way... That light!

01:22.874 --> 01:24.459
Did you make it?

01:25.126 --> 01:26.419
Senku...

01:27.629 --> 01:29.088
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA "JUMP COMICS"

03:17.238 --> 03:19.282
That damnable light...

03:21.284 --> 03:23.745
The world is coming to an end!

03:24.329 --> 03:26.789
Corn City, and this place too!

03:27.373 --> 03:31.084
<i>Also Ruri... and Soyuz...</i>

03:31.085 --> 03:33.421
<i>Everyone will be turned to stone!</i>

03:34.088 --> 03:35.964
<i>A blowout in North America?</i>

03:35.965 --> 03:38.592
<i>No, that's impossible!</i>

03:38.593 --> 03:42.430
<i>This is an ultimate counterattack
to reverse the petrification!</i>

03:53.441 --> 03:57.612
<i>Suika and Francois were sent out
to bring everyone back from petrification.</i>

03:59.322 --> 04:00.823
<i>That's why they've got...</i>

04:01.532 --> 04:05.828
The Revival Fluid
is in the backpacks they took from us!

04:09.582 --> 04:11.541
They destroyed
Senku's last vial of Revival Fluid!

04:11.542 --> 04:13.127
We have to get these...

04:14.545 --> 04:16.213
Exactly.

04:16.214 --> 04:20.635
This is the last Noah's Ark,
the one we call the Revival Fluid.

04:30.061 --> 04:33.273
The rescue took about 100 days.

04:34.357 --> 04:36.942
I thought you'd be faster.

04:36.943 --> 04:39.569
Have you been slacking off, Stan?

04:39.570 --> 04:42.990
The captive princess was the scientist
you've been stuck with all this time.

04:42.991 --> 04:44.908
Shut it.

04:44.909 --> 04:48.161
How about a little heartfelt appreciation?

04:48.162 --> 04:50.456
The petrification beam is coming.

04:54.252 --> 04:56.962
Isn't that the petrification beam?

04:56.963 --> 04:58.965
The same one from thousands of years ago!

04:59.674 --> 05:01.633
If we throw the Revival Fluid
over our heads,

05:01.634 --> 05:03.927
we might have a chance at revival.

05:03.928 --> 05:05.888
That's right.

05:08.683 --> 05:12.729
I'm pretty cool,
so I can show you how, but...

05:17.358 --> 05:18.609
‎Oh crap!

05:19.319 --> 05:22.280
There's no way I could throw it
perfectly at this speed!

05:34.709 --> 05:38.420
Our only chance is to throw a large amount
of Revival Fluid right over our heads.

05:38.421 --> 05:41.214
Assuming the beam's speed
is the same as last time,

05:41.215 --> 05:43.592
the time from when it rises
on the horizon until it arrives--

05:43.593 --> 05:44.718
They're gone!

05:44.719 --> 05:47.013
The Revival Fluid vials are gone!

06:09.368 --> 06:14.749
<i>Why are they putting the Revival Fluid
on Medusa Tower's sound receptacle?</i>

06:15.583 --> 06:19.252
The sound of this shock cannon
is unbelievable!

06:19.253 --> 06:21.881
Even the saucer got cracked...

06:26.094 --> 06:28.763
That's right, Xeno...

06:29.847 --> 06:33.183
<i>Humanity will be extinct for days...</i>

06:33.184 --> 06:35.185
<i>No, maybe...</i>

06:35.186 --> 06:37.772
<i>It will be extinct for months...</i>

06:38.523 --> 06:41.567
<i>But the cry of a wild animal,
the roar of thunder...</i>

06:42.068 --> 06:44.529
<i>At some point, the sounds of nature...</i>

06:45.780 --> 06:49.325
will make the Revival Fluid pour down.

06:50.326 --> 06:52.370
Get the last vial of Revival Fluid!

06:55.206 --> 06:59.627
Damn... I can't move
a single inch of my body...

07:03.381 --> 07:04.757
Suika!

07:05.967 --> 07:12.223
You're the only one
who can get right under Medusa Tower...

07:14.392 --> 07:17.311
You're going to help us, right?

07:41.210 --> 07:43.087
See you, Xeno.

07:43.754 --> 07:46.715
In a few days, or a few years...

07:46.716 --> 07:52.305
Until we meet again,
the day humanity is revived...

07:59.312 --> 08:01.438
<i>It may seem that Senku's side will win</i>

08:01.439 --> 08:05.985
<i>once the Revival Fluid is poured
on his friends after the petrification.</i>

08:06.736 --> 08:12.700
<i>But if I fire now and strike the vial,</i>

08:13.326 --> 08:18.206
<i>the Revival Fluid will spill,
and humanity will be gone for good.</i>

08:18.956 --> 08:23.211
<i>Luckily if it were to hit one of us,
we'd have a chance of winning.</i>

08:23.794 --> 08:26.505
<i>Not shooting means certain defeat.</i>

08:26.506 --> 08:29.799
<i>Doing so, at the cost
of humanity's near-certain extinction,</i>

08:29.800 --> 08:31.636
<i>gives us a small chance of victory...</i>

08:37.808 --> 08:40.394
<i>It's the same great disaster
from thousands of years ago.</i>

08:41.604 --> 08:45.106
<i>Fifty-six seconds between
seeing it on the horizon and its arrival.</i>

08:45.107 --> 08:47.527
<i>It's a perfect recreation.</i>

08:49.862 --> 08:52.865
What an elegant, destructive light!

08:53.616 --> 08:57.870
<i>All the fools who had no interest
in the beauty of new scientific methods</i>

08:58.621 --> 09:01.623
<i>and only sought power and conflict</i>

09:01.624 --> 09:03.334
<i>were just in the way.</i>

09:04.335 --> 09:05.585
Senku...

09:05.586 --> 09:08.713
You and I could have
taken over the new world

09:08.714 --> 09:11.717
and guided it in the right direction.

09:14.595 --> 09:16.096
<i>That's right.</i>

09:16.097 --> 09:19.850
<i>From the very beginning,
we were very much alike.</i>

09:21.644 --> 09:25.815
I wonder why we never
went down the same path.

09:27.191 --> 09:31.696
I told you, ten years ago...

09:32.363 --> 09:37.243
I have zero interest in dictatorships.

09:38.202 --> 09:42.248
We're being ridiculously greedy.

09:43.916 --> 09:46.960
Trying to completely craft
the world of the future,

09:46.961 --> 09:50.131
rather than just
taking the world as it is...

09:51.257 --> 09:55.636
<i>This is tempting...</i>

09:56.554 --> 09:58.722
<i>So, in the end,</i>

09:58.723 --> 10:03.561
<i>you were greedier than us, Senku.</i>

10:04.145 --> 10:05.563
<i>I see!</i>

10:06.147 --> 10:09.066
<i>They were also after Xeno's knowledge.</i>

10:09.567 --> 10:11.068
<i>Congrats.</i>

10:11.652 --> 10:13.236
<i>Even if we're all petrified,</i>

10:13.237 --> 10:16.574
<i>they'll bring back Xeno
and carry on with their science</i>

10:17.366 --> 10:22.663
<i>in exchange for being held hostage forever
as a stone statue.</i>

10:38.429 --> 10:43.601
<i>You won... didn't you?</i>

10:47.021 --> 10:48.522
That light...!

10:52.943 --> 10:56.906
Thank you for your teachings, Dad.

10:57.698 --> 11:01.494
Everyone! Brace yourselves
to avoid breaking while petrified!

11:27.478 --> 11:31.941
<i>On that day, all of humanity...</i>

11:33.234 --> 11:34.902
<i>turned to stone.</i>

16:07.633 --> 16:09.593
Finally...

16:12.262 --> 16:14.847
I made it back from petrification!

16:14.848 --> 16:17.935
Everyone! Senku!

16:24.775 --> 16:28.654
Could it be... that I'm the only one?

16:29.655 --> 16:31.448
This is insanely important.

16:32.408 --> 16:35.452
You'll be the one splitting off, Suika.

16:36.495 --> 16:38.079
That's right!

16:38.080 --> 16:41.333
We failed and got caught.
Then a lot happened...

16:43.335 --> 16:47.588
After everything, I finally took on
the role of the reviver!

16:47.589 --> 16:50.175
I'm being helpful!

16:51.176 --> 16:55.180
I wonder how much time has passed
since that massive petrification beam.

16:55.764 --> 16:58.224
One year? Maybe two years?

16:58.225 --> 17:01.186
I have to pour
the Revival Fluid on everyone--

17:05.024 --> 17:06.692
The Revival Fluid...

17:07.192 --> 17:08.193
Where is it?

17:12.990 --> 17:17.786
First of all,
everything's blurry without my glasses.

17:23.667 --> 17:26.295
I didn't fall this time.

17:37.514 --> 17:39.433
That was close.

17:44.104 --> 17:47.649
This is nothing at all!

17:52.738 --> 17:55.365
I think they were...

17:57.034 --> 17:58.660
over here!

18:03.040 --> 18:05.959
Next, I have to look for
the Revival Fluid!

18:16.553 --> 18:20.307
<i>Senku doesn't have
any more Revival Fluid either.</i>

18:23.811 --> 18:25.229
<i>This one's empty too.</i>

18:28.816 --> 18:30.400
<i>There's none left.</i>

18:38.575 --> 18:41.537
<i>The bit poured on me was the last of it.</i>

18:42.538 --> 18:44.122
<i>There's none left.</i>

18:44.123 --> 18:45.207
<i>All gone.</i>

18:46.125 --> 18:49.753
<i>I can't find Revival Fluid anywhere...</i>

19:25.497 --> 19:29.042
<i>I'll be hungry all the time.</i>

19:30.252 --> 19:33.422
<i>When this leftover food runs out,</i>

19:34.256 --> 19:37.301
<i>my stomach will shrink, and...</i>

19:39.303 --> 19:42.014
<i>I'll die...</i>

19:42.639 --> 19:44.641
<i>all alone...</i>

20:00.908 --> 20:04.328
Wake up! Everyone!

20:04.912 --> 20:08.415
Make something to eat, Francois!

20:08.916 --> 20:14.337
Tell me what to do, Senku!

20:14.338 --> 20:19.092
Hug me, Kohaku!

20:19.718 --> 20:21.553
I can't do it...

20:22.387 --> 20:25.891
I can't stay all alone in this world...

20:46.453 --> 20:52.542
At this moment,
I'm the only human being on Earth.

20:54.628 --> 20:58.840
Senku was all alone too, at the beginning.

20:59.883 --> 21:03.136
Even though no one might ever come back...

21:07.307 --> 21:09.350
But I know one thing.

21:09.351 --> 21:10.978
I'm sure of it.

21:11.937 --> 21:13.563
I know they can wake up.

21:14.523 --> 21:16.566
I just have to find the Revival Fluid.

21:20.112 --> 21:22.030
I'll find everyone's statues!

21:22.906 --> 21:26.117
Maybe someone's got more Revival Fluid!

21:26.118 --> 21:31.623
I'll gather everyone who got scattered,
no matter how long it takes!

22:00.819 --> 22:02.403
<i>What's with that monkey?</i>

22:02.404 --> 22:04.823
<i>Her face alone is all shiny and smooth.</i>

22:05.407 --> 22:08.952
I guess this is the first time
you've seen me, right?

22:10.579 --> 22:12.372
I'm a human!

22:13.165 --> 22:15.959
FOOD, CLOTHES AND SHELTER ACQUIRED!!

